     sseessuuttiill ssttaattuuss [----lliibbxxoo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseessuuttiill utility can be used to query and modify various parameter of
     SCSI Enclosure Services (SES) devices.

     List of supported commands:

     ffaauulltt [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N] _d_i_s_k|aallll oonn|ooffff
             Change the state of the external fault LED associated with _d_i_s_k.
             _d_i_s_k can be the device name of the disk, like ‘da12’, or aallll to
             indicate all disks attached to SES controllers.

     ffaauulltt --uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N _s_e_s_i_d oonn|ooffff
             Change the state of the external fault LED associated with an el‐
             ement connected to the SES controller.  _s_e_s_i_d must be the element
             ID of a valid item attached to the controller.  Use the mmaapp com‐
             mand to list the elements attached to a controller.

     llooccaattee [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N] _d_i_s_k|aallll oonn|ooffff
             Change the state of the external locate LED associated with _d_i_s_k.
             _d_i_s_k can be the device name of the disk, like ‘da12’, or aallll to
             indicate all disks attached to SES controllers.

     llooccaattee --uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N _s_e_s_i_d oonn|ooffff
             Change the state of the external locate LED associated with an
             element connected to the SES controller.  _s_e_s_i_d must be the ele‐
             ment ID of a valid item attached to the controller.  Use the mmaapp
             command to list the elements attached to a controller.

     mmaapp [----lliibbxxoo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N]
             Display a map of all elements connected to the specified ses(4)
             controller.  If no controller is specified, all controllers are
             mapped.

     sshhooww [----lliibbxxoo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N]
             Display user-friendly summary of specified ses(4) controller.  If
             no controller is specified, all controllers are mapped.

     ssttaattuuss [----lliibbxxoo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--uu _/_d_e_v_/_s_e_s_N]
             Display the status of the specified ses(4) controller.  If no
             controller is specified, the status of each controller is re‐
             turned.

     Common options:

     ----lliibbxxoo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s
             Generate output via libxo(3) in a selection of different human
             and machine readable formats.  See xo_parse_args(3)

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Turn off all locate LEDs:

           sseessuuttiill llooccaattee aallll ooffff

     Turn on the locate LED for the drive bay corresponding to _d_a_1_5:

           sseessuuttiill llooccaattee ddaa1155 oonn

     Turn on the fault LED for a drive bay not associated with a device:

           sseessuuttiill ffaauulltt --uu //ddeevv//sseess22 77 oonn

